{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
'''Group 1 of the [[1950 FIFA World Cup]]''' took place from 24 June to 2 July 1950. The group consisted of [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]], [[Yugoslavia national football team|Yugoslavia]], and [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2013/m=12/news=brazil-first-world-cup-draw-2238709.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140614002515/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2013/m=12/news=brazil-first-world-cup-draw-2238709.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=14 June 2014 |title=Brazil's first World Cup draw |date=3 December 2013 |publisher=FIFA}}</ref> The group winners advanced to the [[1950 FIFA World Cup#Final round|final round]].

